comment.body:
[P2] This loop still makes `toPortableMarkdown` take about 1.55 seconds for a 32 KiB input:

```ts
const eol = '\r\n';
const markdown = 'a' + eol + eol.repeat(16384)
	+ '\t' + eol + eol + '[open](file:///fixture.ts)';
toPortableMarkdown(markdown);
```

The lexer expands the tab, so this whitespace token cannot match. Its first line is empty, which makes the outer loop try every source offset and rescan almost the same newline suffix each time. Doubling the blank-line count roughly quadruples the runtime. LF input also regresses.

The exact base implementation takes under 1 ms on the same input. Copy, Copy All and Copy Final Response invoke this transformation synchronously before writing the clipboard. Could the locator avoid these overlapping rescans and cover a long unmatched whitespace token?

These are measurements of the production transformation in Electron on macOS arm64; I haven't exercised the full clipboard UI flow.

