comment.body:
**[P2] Avoid rescanning the shared indicator prefix for each caret**

`deleteLeft` calls this once per caret, so carets near the end of a long regional-indicator run repeatedly scan the same prefix. With one 512 KiB line (`'🇺🇸'.repeat(65536)`) and carets after its last 8,192 flags, one synchronous Backspace takes **2.36–2.51 s at this head versus 0.91–0.94 s at merge-base `3d7cfab6`** on an M5 Pro. This uses the real `CoreEditingCommands.DeleteLeft` through `withTestCodeEditor` in Chromium 149, within the default 10,000-cursor limit.

The head correctly deletes whole flags and undo succeeds in both versions. The smaller all-flags case is faster at head; the slowdown here specifically comes from the long untouched prefix. Computing pairing boundaries/parity once per affected line or deletion operation would avoid repeated prefix scans while retaining the odd-run case.

The bounded editor setup is:

```ts
const flag = '🇺🇸';
withTestCodeEditor(flag.repeat(65536), {}, editor => {
	editor.setSelections(Array.from({ length: 8192 }, (_, i) => {
		const column = (57344 + i + 1) * flag.length + 1;
		return new Selection(1, column, 1, column);
	}));
	editor.runCommand(CoreEditingCommands.DeleteLeft, null);
});
```

