I found another case where the filtered mask affects a newly spawned deferred task. Two suspended transitions increment separate state queues, then a third transition increments both. When an older lazy module resolves during the combined retry, the spawned task omits one entangled increment and commits `Ready 2:1Final 2:1`, even though the desired `2:2` resources are still pending.

The base keeps `Ready 0:0` until `Final 2:2` resolves. This is an incorrect intermediate commit; the later update can still reach `2:2`.

The identical test passes on complete base `76baa3b5434fad315ece9cfd4d20d7a8d6c34a25` and fails on complete head `6c4ad547b0f7eafe8d1567d0d5c013417130b825` in eight configurations: experimental/stable development and production, plus both www variants in development and production. The head's other 24 deferred-value tests pass. Keeping the complete spawned-task dependency mask separately makes all 25 pass, including this PR's two new cases.

These are source-renderer tests using Node 24.22.1; the historical revisions pin Node 20.19.0.


